            <ownedLogicalComponents xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.la:LogicalComponent"
                id="f7120182-ca89-493f-8a70-9d197301b4e6" name="Goverance Layer" description="&lt;p>&lt;strong>Governance Layer&lt;/strong> realizes &lt;em data-end=&quot;4974&quot; data-start=&quot;4943&quot;>Audit and Policy Enforcement.&lt;/em>&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>What&amp;rsquo;s Implemented (Structural / Conceptual)&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Capella Model:&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>The Governance Layer is a top-level logical component supervising the Decision &amp;amp; Reasoning Core, Contract Manager, and Context Memory.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Control exchanges (policy, audit, oversight) are already modeled in YAML.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Design Intent:&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>You&amp;rsquo;ve defined the Governance Layer as the agent&amp;rsquo;s &amp;ldquo;safety net&amp;rdquo;: ensuring decisions comply with defined rules or evaluation metrics.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>It mirrors the &amp;ldquo;policy / oversight&amp;rdquo; layer in AgentSquare or UMF frameworks.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>🧩 How You Could Introduce Governance Incrementally&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>LevelDescriptionExample Implementation&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Level 1 &amp;ndash; Policy HooksCreate a simple governance.py module that inspects messages before and after a tool runs.Example: check if prompt contains disallowed keywords, or if JSON schema validation passes.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Level 2 &amp;ndash; Audit TrailExtend your existing trace mechanism (Context Memory &amp;amp; Trace Store) to log contract transitions, selected tools, and reasoning results.Store governance entries in a structured JSON (e.g., &amp;quot;decision_log&amp;quot;: { &amp;quot;tool&amp;quot;: ..., &amp;quot;policy_check&amp;quot;: ... }).&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Level 3 &amp;ndash; Evaluation FeedbackAdd an LLM call or a rule engine that reviews outputs for correctness, tone, or completeness.For instance, evaluate_output(prompt, response) returning `&amp;quot;pass&amp;quot;&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Level 4 &amp;ndash; Meta-ControlEnable the Governance Layer to block or reroute actions (e.g., reject a risky tool invocation).Integrate a simple decision gate in your orchestrator: if governance.approves(decision): run_tool().&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Governance Layer in Your Architecture Context&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>In Capella terms, this becomes:&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Function: Evaluate Decision Compliance&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Exchange: Governance Policy &amp;rarr; Contract Manager&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Exchange: Audit Log &amp;rarr; Trace Store&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Function allocation: Governance Layer realizes &amp;ldquo;Evaluate Output Quality&amp;rdquo; and &amp;ldquo;Approve Contract Transition.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>🔜 Practical Next Step&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>I suggest you start with a Governance Hook Class like this:&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>class GovernanceLayer: def __init__(self): self.policies = {&amp;quot;max_tokens&amp;quot;: 4000, &amp;quot;require_json_output&amp;quot;: True} def approve(self, decision): # Example policy: require structured JSON decisions if self.policies.get(&amp;quot;require_json_output&amp;quot;) and not decision.strip().startswith(&amp;quot;{&amp;quot;): return False, &amp;quot;Decision not in JSON format&amp;quot; return True, &amp;quot;Approved&amp;quot; def audit(self, event_type, details): print(f&amp;quot;[GOVERNANCE] {event_type}: {details}&amp;quot;)&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Then call it in your orchestrator:&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>approved, msg = governance.approve(agent_decision) if not approved: governance.audit(&amp;quot;Rejection&amp;quot;, msg) return &amp;quot;Governance rejection: &amp;quot; + msg&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Would you like me to help you design a Level 1 governance module (lightweight policy + audit hook) that integrates into your existing ChatGPTAnalyzer or SE Agent loop?&lt;br />&#xA;It would be the first working embodiment of your Capella Governance Layer.&lt;/p>&#xA;">
              <ownedFeatures xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.fa:ComponentPort"
                  id="533c4272-ce29-4ab0-89b4-2004a5454b28" name="CP 1" orientation="OUT"
                  kind="FLOW"/>
              <ownedFeatures xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.fa:ComponentPort"
                  id="56665358-cd57-4f52-9961-d16f3b1010a7" name="CP 2" orientation="OUT"
                  kind="FLOW"/>
              <ownedFeatures xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.fa:ComponentPort"
                  id="2c6224ac-21ad-4f50-98f5-575c959e159d" name="CP 3" orientation="OUT"
                  kind="FLOW"/>
              <ownedFeatures xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.fa:ComponentPort"
                  id="7f2c97df-2077-440d-a66f-b156caa063cf" name="CP 4" orientation="OUT"
                  kind="FLOW"/>
            </ownedLogicalComponents>
