                name="work space manager" abstractType="#cd885340-ac19-486e-b903-d643de5e9ce8"/>
            <ownedLogicalComponents xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.la:LogicalComponent"
                id="085e223e-cc0d-453c-aecc-0493db782c61" name="Knowledge Repo " description="&lt;h2>&lt;span style=&quot;color:#3b3b3b&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;,Roboto,sans-serif&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8f8f8&quot;>Artifact Repository MCP &amp;mdash; Service Summary&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/h2>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;color:#3b3b3b&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;,Roboto,sans-serif&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8f8f8&quot;>A FastMCP server (&lt;code>kp/artifact_repo/server.py&lt;/code>, port 8002, &lt;code>streamable-http&lt;/code> transport at &lt;code>POST /mcp&lt;/code>) that exposes &lt;strong>CRUD operations over Pydantic-typed, git-backed artifacts&lt;/strong> stored in a GitHub repo. Everything is session-scoped: clone a repo to get a &lt;code>session_id&lt;/code>, operate on it, then push and clean up.&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3>&lt;span style=&quot;color:#3b3b3b&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;,Roboto,sans-serif&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8f8f8&quot;>Session lifecycle&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/h3>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul>&#xA;&#x9;&lt;li>&lt;strong>&lt;code>clone_artifact_repo(remote_url, pat, branch)&lt;/code>&lt;/strong>&amp;nbsp;&amp;mdash; clones a GitHub repo (PAT injected into the HTTPS URL, scrubbed from error output) into a temp dir on the server, wraps it in a&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>GitStore&lt;/code>, and returns a&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>session_id&lt;/code>. Must be called first.&lt;/li>&#xA;&#x9;&lt;li>&lt;strong>&lt;code>cleanup_session(session_id)&lt;/code>&lt;/strong>&amp;nbsp;&amp;mdash; deletes the local clone and frees the session.&lt;/li>&#xA;&lt;/ul>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3>&lt;span style=&quot;color:#3b3b3b&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;,Roboto,sans-serif&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8f8f8&quot;>CRUD / discovery (backed by&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:large&quot;>&lt;code>GitStore&lt;/code>&lt;/span>&amp;nbsp;&amp;rarr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:large&quot;>FilesystemStore&lt;/span>&lt;/code>, auto-committing on every write/delete)&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/h3>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul>&#xA;&#x9;&lt;li>&lt;strong>&lt;code>list_artifact_packages&lt;/code>&lt;/strong>&amp;nbsp;&amp;mdash; list package names in the repo.&lt;/li>&#xA;&#x9;&lt;li>&lt;strong>&lt;code>browse_artifact_repo&lt;/code>&lt;/strong>&amp;nbsp;&amp;mdash; list artifact metadata in a package, filterable by type/name substring, with a result limit.&lt;/li>&#xA;&#x9;&lt;li>&lt;strong>&lt;code>read_artifact&lt;/code>&lt;/strong>&amp;nbsp;&amp;mdash; fetch one artifact&amp;#39;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>metadata&lt;/code>,&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>content_str&lt;/code>, and&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>type&lt;/code>&amp;nbsp;by ID.&lt;/li>&#xA;&#x9;&lt;li>&lt;strong>&lt;code>write_artifact&lt;/code>&lt;/strong>&amp;nbsp;&amp;mdash; create or overwrite an artifact (package auto-created); content format depends on&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>type&lt;/code>&amp;nbsp;(CSV for&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>table&lt;/code>, YAML for&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>yaml&lt;/code>/&lt;code>arcadia_fabric&lt;/code>, Markdown for&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>text&lt;/code>/&lt;code>session_summary&lt;/code>, JSON for others); supports tags,&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>source_tool&lt;/code>, and&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>lineage&lt;/code>&amp;nbsp;(parent artifact IDs) for traceability.&lt;/li>&#xA;&#x9;&lt;li>&lt;strong>&lt;code>delete_artifact&lt;/code>&lt;/strong>&amp;nbsp;&amp;mdash; remove an artifact (also git-removes its files and commits).&lt;/li>&#xA;&#x9;&lt;li>&lt;strong>&lt;code>get_artifact_versions&lt;/code>&lt;/strong>&amp;nbsp;&amp;mdash; git commit history (&lt;code>commit&lt;/code>,&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>timestamp&lt;/code>,&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>message&lt;/code>) for a given artifact.&lt;/li>&#xA;&#x9;&lt;li>&lt;strong>&lt;code>search_artifacts&lt;/code>&lt;/strong>&amp;nbsp;&amp;mdash; case-insensitive full-text search across names, tags, and content, with optional type filter.&lt;/li>&#xA;&lt;/ul>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3>&lt;span style=&quot;color:#3b3b3b&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;,Roboto,sans-serif&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8f8f8&quot;>Branching (the change reviewed earlier in this session)&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/h3>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul>&#xA;&#x9;&lt;li>&lt;strong>&lt;code>list_artifact_branches&lt;/code>&lt;/strong>&amp;nbsp;&amp;mdash; lists remote branches (via&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>git branch -r&lt;/code>,&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>origin/&lt;/code>&amp;nbsp;prefix stripped).&lt;/li>&#xA;&#x9;&lt;li>&lt;strong>&lt;code>create_artifact_branch&lt;/code>&lt;/strong>&amp;nbsp;&amp;mdash; creates a new branch from the session clone&amp;#39;s current HEAD, optionally pushing it upstream immediately.&lt;/li>&#xA;&lt;/ul>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3>&lt;span style=&quot;color:#3b3b3b&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;,Roboto,sans-serif&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8f8f8&quot;>Prompt rendering&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/h3>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul>&#xA;&#x9;&lt;li>&lt;strong>&lt;code>render_prompt&lt;/code>&lt;/strong>&amp;nbsp;&amp;mdash; finds a&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>prompt_def&lt;/code>&amp;nbsp;artifact by name in a package, renders it with Jinja2 against supplied variables, and optionally saves the rendered output as a&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>prompt&lt;/code>&amp;nbsp;artifact with lineage back to the&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>prompt_def&lt;/code>.&lt;/li>&#xA;&lt;/ul>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3>&lt;span style=&quot;color:#3b3b3b&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;,Roboto,sans-serif&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8f8f8&quot;>Sync&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/h3>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul>&#xA;&#x9;&lt;li>&lt;strong>&lt;code>push_artifacts&lt;/code>&lt;/strong>&amp;nbsp;&amp;mdash; pushes all locally committed artifacts back to the remote GitHub repo (call before&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>cleanup_session&lt;/code>&amp;nbsp;to persist work).&lt;/li>&#xA;&lt;/ul>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3>&lt;span style=&quot;color:#3b3b3b&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;,Roboto,sans-serif&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8f8f8&quot;>Registered artifact types&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/h3>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;color:#3b3b3b&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;,Roboto,sans-serif&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8f8f8&quot;>&lt;code>arcadia_fabric&lt;/code>, &lt;code>json&lt;/code>, &lt;code>prompt&lt;/code>, &lt;code>prompt_def&lt;/code>, &lt;code>session_summary&lt;/code>, &lt;code>table&lt;/code>, &lt;code>text&lt;/code>, &lt;code>yaml&lt;/code> (registry in registry.py, extensible at runtime via &lt;code>register_artifact_type&lt;/code>).&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3>&lt;span style=&quot;color:#3b3b3b&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;,Roboto,sans-serif&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8f8f8&quot;>Notable design points&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/h3>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul>&#xA;&#x9;&lt;li>&lt;code>GitStore&lt;/code>&amp;nbsp;(git_store.py) auto-commits on every write/delete with descriptive messages, but never auto-pushes &amp;mdash;&amp;nbsp;&lt;code>push_artifacts&lt;/code>&amp;nbsp;is explicit.&lt;/li>&#xA;&#x9;&lt;li>Transport security restricts allowed hosts (&lt;code>repo.innovatingwithcapella.com&lt;/code>, localhost variants) with DNS-rebinding protection enabled.&lt;/li>&#xA;&#x9;&lt;li>Degrades gracefully to plain filesystem behavior if the cloned directory isn&amp;#39;t a real git repo (&lt;code>_git_ok&lt;/code>&amp;nbsp;guard).&lt;/li>&#xA;&lt;/ul>&#xA;">
              <ownedFunctionalAllocation xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.fa:ComponentFunctionalAllocation"
